# Example ReRDMFT input file: LiH, 6-31G, GNOF, READ_OCCUPANCIES TRUE -- reads OCC.in (this
# directory's own companion file) instead of running the usual LBFGS(gamma) occupation-number
# optimization at the starting HF orbitals: "index" is the PNOF subspace (0 or 1, matching
# PNOF_SUBSPACES 2 below), the two lines per subspace are that subspace's principal geminal (the
# larger value) then its one virtual (PNOF_COUPLING 2), summing to 1 per subspace. Watch for
# "READ_OCCUPANCIES TRUE: occupations read directly from OCC.in ... did NOT run" and the printed
# occupation numbers matching OCC.in's own values exactly, and the RESTART file's own
# self-consistency check ("gamma angles regenerate the occupation numbers") still passing --
# confirming the occupations-to-gammas conversion is exact for externally-supplied occupations
# too, not just ones this project's own optimizer produced.
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2
READ_OCCUPANCIES TRUE
USE_RI FALSE  # preserve this example's pre-existing dense/Cholesky path (USE_RI now defaults TRUE)

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
